distroforge (0.3.5-15) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The signing key now carries a user id for the address debian/control
    publishes. That was the one gap docs/packaging-release.md recorded as
    still open: the Maintainer field named github@distroforge.anonaddy.com
    while the key had no user id for it, so a keyring exported for an apt
    repository would have authenticated the archive without naming the
    maintainer it belongs to. Added with gpg --quick-add-uid, which needs
    the maintainer's own passphrase; the documented export filter already
    accepted that address, so no procedure changed.
  * Re-measured the documented export, because adding a user id moves every
    number in it: the whole key is now 3579 bytes with three user ids, the
    filtered form 2930 bytes with the two published ones, and the personal
    mailbox is still excluded. The filtered export imported into an empty
    GNUPGHOME verifies real signatures -- git verify-commit returns 0 on
    two commits of this branch -- while a keyring with nothing imported
    returns 1, which is what makes the 0 evidence about the export rather
    than about an ambient keyring.
  * Recorded one consequence instead of leaving it to be discovered: gpg
    treats the most recently self-signed user id as primary, so that alias
    is now the identity gpg prints for a signature made by this key, and
    debsign can select the key from a changelog trailer. The copy GitHub
    holds is unaffected -- it stores what was uploaded, the noreply user id
    is still on it, and commit verification there is unchanged.
  * The figures in 0.3.5-14 are deliberately left as written. A changelog
    entry records the state at its own version, so it is superseded here
    rather than rewritten.

