distroforge (0.3.5-9) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Enforce the promise that the maintainer address stamped into generated .deb
    packages tracks debian/control. _DEB_MAINTAINER in core/desktop_source.py is
    printed straight into the DEBIAN/control of every desktop component package
    the tool assembles, so it reaches end users rather than staying inside this
    source tree, and a comment claiming it was "kept in step with the Maintainer
    field of debian/control" was the only thing holding the two together. That
    is the shape that goes stale in silence: correcting one site leaves the
    other behind, and the divergence surfaces in a stranger's package.
  * The new guard asserts that the two agree rather than what they say, so it
    survives the address changing and fails only if a change misses a site.
    Verified to fail on a deliberately desynchronised constant.
  * Recorded while auditing archive readiness: the address is currently
    maintainers@distroforge.invalid, which Debian Policy 5.6.2 does not allow
    for an upload, and which no lintian check catches. bogus-mail-host fires
    only when the host is not a domain, and Net::Domain::TLD counts .invalid as
    a domain because it is an RFC 2606 reserved TLD present in that list;
    mail-address-loops-or-bounces knows exactly one address, unrelated. So the
    package lints clean, builds clean and is still not uploadable. Fixing the
    address is a separate change and needs a deliverable one to exist first.

